%% UC-29 — Run a backup (backup-service, daily loop after startup delay, or
%% triggered manually / as a pre-restore safety snapshot via the admin UI)
%% Source: backup-service/backup.sh, backup-service/lib.sh, docker-compose.yml
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CR as backup-service (daily loop, or backup-api on demand)
    participant LK as Shared lock (mkdir /backups/.lock)
    participant M as MongoDB
    participant LR as LightRAG (volume)
    participant N4 as Neo4j
    participant KC as Keycloak
    participant FS as Backup volume (./backups)
    participant WH as Alert webhook / email

    Note over CR: BACKUP_TRIGGER = scheduled | manual | pre_restore_safety
    CR->>LK: acquire_lock (fails fast, steals a stale lock from a dead PID)
    alt lock held by a live process
        LK-->>CR: refuse — another backup/restore is already running
    end
    CR->>M: mongodump --archive
    M-->>CR: dump stream (sets MONGO_OK)
    CR->>LR: tar -czf lightrag-data.tar.gz (read-only volume mount)
    LR-->>CR: archive (sets LIGHTRAG_OK)
    CR->>N4: docker stop hhh-neo4j + neo4j-admin database dump (via docker.sock)
    N4-->>CR: graph dump, container restarted (sets NEO4J_OK)
    CR->>KC: realm partial-export (realm hhh)
    KC-->>CR: realm JSON (sets KEYCLOAK_OK, or KEYCLOAK_SKIPPED if no credentials)
    CR->>FS: Write full_backup_<DATE>.tar.gz + backup_<DATE>.manifest (human) + .manifest.json (structured, per-component flags — read by the admin UI's status endpoint)
    CR->>FS: Prune backups/manifests older than BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS (default 14)
    CR->>LK: release_lock
    alt any step failed
        CR->>WH: Failure alert (ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL / ALERT_EMAIL)
    end
